## One expressive type moment: kinetic variable weight

Allowed once per page, on the primary display headline only. As the hero settles or as the reader scrolls it into place, the headline shifts weight along its variable axis. This is the structural use of the 2026 kinetic type trend: the motion is the type asserting itself, not an ornament bolted on. Gate it behind reduced motion and keep it to one element.

```css
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
  @supports (animation-timeline: view()) {
    .display-kinetic {
      animation: weight-settle linear both;
      animation-timeline: view();
      animation-range: entry 0% entry 50%;
    }
    @keyframes weight-settle {
      from { font-variation-settings: "wght" 300; }
      to   { font-variation-settings: "wght" 720; }
    }
  }
}
```

Never apply this to body text. Never to more than one element. Never as an infinite loop.

