## Toggled content: @starting-style, not JavaScript classes

For anything that enters by toggling `display` (menus, dialogs, popovers, accordions), use `@starting-style` with `transition-behavior: allow-discrete`. No JavaScript added classes, no setTimeout. Baseline since August 2024. Non supporting browsers simply show the content without the animation.

```css
.overlay-menu, dialog {
  opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0);
  transition:
    opacity 300ms var(--ease-out-soft),
    transform 300ms var(--ease-out-soft),
    display 300ms allow-discrete,
    overlay 300ms allow-discrete;
}
@starting-style {
  .overlay-menu, dialog { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(8px); }
}
.overlay-menu[hidden], dialog:not([open]) { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(8px); }
```

This pairs directly with the anchor positioned, Popover API menus from the design language document. Anchor positioning places the menu, the Popover API opens and closes it, and `@starting-style` animates the entrance. Zero positioning or toggling JavaScript.

