## Scroll reveals

Every content block that enters the viewport animates in once and stays. Children stagger so they cascade rather than arrive together. Two layers.

**Baseline: Intersection Observer.** Works everywhere, around 98 percent support. The production safe default.

```tsx
// hooks/useInView.ts
'use client'
import { useEffect, useRef, useState } from 'react'
export function useInView(options?: IntersectionObserverInit) {
  const ref = useRef<HTMLElement>(null)
  const [inView, setInView] = useState(false)
  useEffect(() => {
    const el = ref.current
    if (!el) return
    const observer = new IntersectionObserver(([entry]) => {
      if (entry.isIntersecting) { setInView(true); observer.unobserve(el) }
    }, { threshold: 0.15, rootMargin: '0px 0px -40px 0px', ...options })
    observer.observe(el)
    return () => observer.disconnect()
  }, [])
  return { ref, inView }
}
```

**Progressive enhancement: CSS scroll driven animations** (`animation-timeline: view()`). Shipped in Chrome and Safari. Firefox still gates it behind a flag as of mid-2026, and it is on the Interop 2026 list, so check support before promoting it past `@supports`. Gate it and let Intersection Observer cover the rest.

```css
@supports (animation-timeline: view()) {
  .reveal-css {
    animation: fade-up-sda linear both;
    animation-timeline: view();
    animation-range: entry 0% entry 60%;
  }
  @keyframes fade-up-sda { from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(32px); } to { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); } }
}
```

When Firefox ships scroll driven animations unflagged, the Intersection Observer layer can be retired. Until then, keep both.

### Reveal behavior by element

- Display headlines: up, 700ms.
- Rule lines: scaleX 0 to 1 from left, 600ms, 50ms after the section enters.
- Body paragraphs: up 20px, 500ms, stagger 80ms per paragraph.
- Images: opacity 0 to 1 with scale 1.03 to 1, 700ms. No translateY on images, so layout does not shift.
- Mosaic images: stagger 80ms to 100ms, left to right or diagonal.
- Stat numbers: count up from 0, 1200ms, with a reduced motion check that sets the final value immediately.
- Sidebar labels: fade only, 400ms, 200ms after the section enters.

